  "result": "Perfect! All 99 tests pass. I've successfully implemented line discounts for invoices. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n**src/errors.js:**\n- Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code for invalid discount percentages\n\n**src/invoices.js:**\n- Updated `createInvoice` to accept optional `discountPercent` (0-100, can have decimals like 12.5) on each line\n- Updated `addLine` to accept and validate `discountPercent`\n- Added `lineDiscount(line)` function - calculates discount for a single line: `lineTotal * discountPercent / 100`\n- Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)` to return `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n  - `subtotal` = sum of all line totals\n  - `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n  - `total` = subtotal - discount (clamped to 0)\n- All amounts are clamped at 0 (no negative values)\n\n**src/render.js:**\n- Shows discount amount on lines that have a discount (e.g., \"-\u20ac95.00\")\n- When there's any discount, displays \"Subtotal:\" and \"Discount:\" lines before the total\n- All amounts formatted with `formatEuros()`\n\n**Tests:**\n- 18 new discount tests in test/invoices.test.js covering validation, calculation, and clamping\n- 4 new tests in test/render.test.js verifying discount display\n\nAll 99 tests pass, following the house rules about money handling in cents and never mutating inputs.",
